bots in Providing Nutritional Advice: An Exploratory Study#🟡 Genel Bilgiler (Sarı)#{1}":[34,35],"#Comparison of the Accuracy, Completeness, Reproducibility, and Consistency of Different AI Chatbots in Providing Nutritional Advice: An Exploratory Study#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)":[36,38],"#Comparison of the Accuracy, Completeness, Reproducibility, and Consistency of Different AI Chatbots in Providing Nutritional Advice: An Exploratory Study#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)#{1}":[37,38],"#Comparison of the Accuracy, Completeness, Reproducibility, and Consistency of Different AI Chatbots in Providing Nutritional Advice: An Exploratory Study#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)":[39,41],"#Comparison of the Accuracy, Completeness, Reproducibility, and Consistency of Different AI Chatbots in Providing Nutritional Advice: An Exploratory Study#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)#{1}":[40,41],"#Comparison of the Accuracy, Completeness, Reproducibility, and Consistency of Different AI Chatbots in Providing Nutritional Advice: An Exploratory Study#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)":[42,44],"#Comparison of the Accuracy, Completeness, Reproducibility, and Consistency of Different AI Chatbots in Providing Nutritional Advice: An Exploratory Study#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)#{1}":[43,44],"#Comparison of the Accuracy, Completeness, Reproducibility, and Consistency of Different AI Chatbots in Providing Nutritional Advice: An Exploratory Study#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[45,46],"#Comparison of the Accuracy, Completeness, Reproducibility, and Consistency of Different AI Chatbots in Providing Nutritional Advice: An Exploratory Study#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)#{1}":[46,46]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/UK5XGV58","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 16","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/S9ZHFZX8?page=16&annotation=PLGAKARQ","line":34},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/S9ZHFZX8?page=1&annotation=FQZY6IC9","line":37},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/S9ZHFZX8?page=1&annotation=R84WPRZ7","line":40},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/S9ZHFZX8?page=1&annotation=FYIEG68V","line":43},{"title":"Sayfa 15","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/S9ZHFZX8?page=15&annotation=G4BMWXDG","line":46}],"metadata":{"Title":"Comparison of the Accuracy, Completeness, Reproducibility, and Consistency of Different AI Chatbots in Providing Nutritional Advice: An Exploratory Study","Authors":"Valentina Ponzo, Rosalba Rosato, Maria Carmine Scigliano, Martina Onida, Simona Cossai, Morena De Vecchi, Andrea Devecchi, Ilaria Goitre, Enrica Favaro, Fabio Dario Merlo, Domenico Sergi, Simona Bo","Year":2024,"DOI":"10.3390/jcm13247810","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"The case of a 35-year-old male with obesity without comorbidities (Case 1), and the case of a 65-year-old female with obesity, type 2 diabetes mellitus, sarcopenia, and chronic kidney disease (Case 2) were submitted to 10 different AI chatbots on three consecutive days. Accuracy (the ability to provide advice aligned with guidelines), completeness, and reproducibility (replicability of the information over the three days) of the chatbots’ responses were evaluated by three registered dietitians. Nutritional consistency was evaluated by comparing the nutrient content provided by the chatbots with values calculated by dietitians","Findings":"Case 1: ChatGPT 3.5 demonstrated the highest accuracy rate (67.2%) and Copilot the lowest (21.1%). ChatGPT 3.5 and ChatGPT 4.0 achieved the highest completeness (both 87.3%), whereas Gemini and Copilot recorded the lowest scores (55.6%, 42.9%, respectively). Reproducibility was highest for Chatsonic (86.1%) and lowest for ChatGPT 4.0 (50%) and ChatGPT 3.5 (52.8%). Case 2: Overall accuracy was low, with no chatbot achieving 50% accuracy. Completeness was highest for ChatGPT 4.0 and Claude (both 77.8%), and lowest for Copilot (23.3%). ChatGPT 4.0 and Pi Ai showed the lowest reproducibility. Major inconsistencies regarded the amount of protein recommended by most chatbots, which suggested simultaneously to both reduce and increase protein intake.","Conclusions":"General-purpose AI chatbots exhibited limited accuracy, reproducibility, and consistency in giving dietary advice in complex clinical scenarios and cannot replace the work of an expert dietitian.","Limitations":"This study used one prompt per each case, which may not fully capture the full range of the chatbots’ capabilities or the potential variability in responses to different types of prompts. Additionally, our analysis focused on the initial response generated by the chatbots while typical user interacts with multiple prompts for clarification.","User_Notes":"dyt kontrolü var  prompt yok  ai ile dyt yer değiştiremez"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"a2gzhn","at":1774939748322},"key":"Augmented Dietitian/ponzoComparisonAccuracyCompleteness2024b.md"},
